    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50538" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰξᾰλῆ</span></b>  (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰξάλη</span> in codd., but <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰξαλῆ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.Dion.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					398
				</span></i>
			), ἡ, <i>goat's skin</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τελείας αἰγὸς δέρμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Erot.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Fract.</u>
				29
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				19.106
			</span></i>; used as a dress for actors in satyric dramas, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				4.118
			</span></i>. (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰζάλη</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰζάνη</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
			</span></i> l.c., <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσάλη</span></b> 
				Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				72
			</span></i>; cf. the forms <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσσέλα</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰτθέλα</span></b> ,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσθλῆ</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσσέλη</span></b> 
			<i><span class="en">
				Theognost.
				<u>Can.</u>
				14
			</span></i>: cf. sq.)</div>
